// Dialog as a true overlay (task 15): the modal consumes no flow space, paints
// last over the page, and dims it with a backdrop scrim. The page below (AppBar +
// content) lays out exactly as if the Dialog were absent; the centered Dialog
// floats on top. A second frame shows a fullScreen dialog filling the screen.
//
// The dialogs are built from the Dialog kit (task 14): DialogHeader (title row),
// DialogContent (padded body), DialogActions (right-aligned button row -- no manual
// Spacer needed, MUI alignment).

Wireframe #page landscape
  AppBar
    Toolbar
      Typography h6 "Projects"
      Spacer
      Icon "Search"
      Avatar "JD"
  Stack column spacing=2
    Typography h5 "Your projects"
    Stack row spacing=2
      Card
        Typography subtitle1 "Apollo"
        Typography body2 "Updated 2 hours ago"
      Card
        Typography subtitle1 "Borealis"
        Typography body2 "Updated yesterday"
      Card
        Typography subtitle1 "Cosmos"
        Typography body2 "Updated last week"
    Typography ~3
  Dialog sm
    DialogHeader "Delete project?"
    DialogContent
      Typography body2 "This permanently removes Apollo and all its data."
    DialogActions
      Button "Cancel"
      Button "Delete" contained to=#page

Wireframe #fullscreen landscape
  AppBar
    Toolbar
      Typography h6 "Settings"
  Stack column spacing=2
    Typography body2 "The page behind is fully covered."
    Typography ~4
  Dialog fullScreen
    DialogHeader "Edit profile"
    DialogContent
      Typography body2 "A full-screen dialog fills the whole frame."
    DialogActions
      Button "Save" contained to=#page
